# variant-set v1.0.0

## Forms

### `(primitive …)`

Primitive assembly state. `:topology` selects the variant; the strip-index-format key exists only under a strip.

| Key | Type | Required | Default | Constraints |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `:topology` | `symbol enum` | no | `triangle-list` | one of: `point-list`, `line-list`, `line-strip`, `triangle-list`, `triangle-strip`<br>Defaults to triangle-list, as GPUPrimitiveState does. |
| `:cull` | `symbol` | no | — | none / front / back. |

#### Variant `:topology [triangle-strip line-strip]`

| Key | Type | Required | Default | Constraints |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `:strip-index-format` | `symbol enum` | no | — | one of: `uint16`, `uint32`<br>The primitive-restart index format; only meaningful when the topology is a strip. |

## Value kinds

### topology

How vertices assemble into primitives: the five WebGPU topologies.

Type: `symbol enum` — one of: `point-list`, `line-list`, `line-strip`, `triangle-list`, `triangle-strip`.

### index-format

The index buffer element type.

Type: `symbol enum` — one of: `uint16`, `uint32`.
